    fix(api): clamp GET /api/v1/problems limit to documented max 100. Addresses OB-GAP-081.
    
    Over-max limit values (101, 200, ...) previously fell back to the
    default 20, silently returning a short page. A new clampIntDefault
    helper clamps values above max to 100; omitted, non-numeric, and
    non-positive values keep the default-20 fallback, and the
    answers/queue endpoints keep parseIntDefault unchanged.
    
    docs/api-reference.md now states the exact boundary behavior, and
    TestListProblems_LimitBoundaries pins 100/101/200/0/-3/abc/omitted
    plus offset pagination across the clamp boundary (RED-proven against
    the pre-fix handler).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
